The Dirty Pipe vulnerability is a Linux kernel vulnerability that was discovered in 2022. It allows an attacker to write arbitrary data to arbitrary files on a Linux system. The vulnerability is present in Linux kernels version 5.8 and later.
The vulnerability is in the pipe_fs.c file of the Linux kernel. The file contains code for the pipe2 system call. The pipe2 system call is used to create a pipe. A pipe is a way for a process to write to and read from a file.
The pipe2 system call does not properly validate the file descriptors that a process uses when calling the system call. As a result, a process can use the pipe2 system call to write to a file descriptor that it does not have write access to. This allows a process to write to arbitrary files.
